{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790191296,"nonce":"g4FL3+IqA+nFZa1ASMzEL4hM3cs=","title":"The generated `gpu` namespace covers basic compute, buffer readback, rendering","message":"and presentation, but does not yet cover the portable WebGPU/wgpu feature set\ndescribed by `plugins/cb_gpu/spec/webgpu.idl`.\n\nMissing groups:\n\n- adapter features and complete limits, plus required feature/limit device negotiation;\n- explicit bind-group and pipeline layouts, dynamic offsets and binding ranges;\n- full texture/view/sampler descriptors, storage textures, dimensions, mips, layers and multisampling;\n- complete format catalogs (105 texture and 42 vertex formats in the vendored IDL; six and four exported now);\n- programmable constants, complete render-pass load/store state and full draw ranges;\n- query sets, timestamps, occlusion, render bundles and external textures/images;\n- error scopes, device-lost events and structured compilation messages;\n- configurable surface usage, present/alpha modes, view formats, color space and latency.\n\nThe target layer is prepared separately: the crate compile-checks for Metal,\nDX12, Vulkan, Android Vulkan/GLES, browser WebGPU and Emscripten GLES. Buffer\nsizes/ranges/offsets and reported limits now remain 64-bit through the Caribou\nABI. Keep this issue about API coverage and add conformance fixtures as groups\nland rather than treating a successful target compile as complete coverage.","files":null}]}